  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Slide 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 3. The metre bridge is a sensitive device that gives the most accurate
    result when the resistance of all four arms of the bridge are of the same order.
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The metre bridge is sensitive when the resistance of all four
    arms of the bridge are of the same order. If we measure too high or too low a
    resistance, the current is too small, and so is the metre deflection which doesn't
    give accurate results.
  options:
  - True
  - False
  - Cannot be determined
  - Both True and False
  correctOptionIndex: 0
